<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>07 · RESULTS (6/6) — H3 AND H4</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        One question we cannot answer, one we can only describe
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 40, marginTop: 22 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 20px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#FF6B6B', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>H3 · INFORMATION VERSUS ARCHITECTURE</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 8, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                A5 is not constructible — it was never merely unrun
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.7 }}>
                Its three pre-registered inputs do not exist in the data: no repeat-count column among the 18,152 structures;
                18,036 wPSMILES all carry the same repeat field <span style={{ color: '#FFFFFF' }}>|1|</span> and one identical weight block;
                one row per repeat unit, so no multi-unit sequence.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 8, lineHeight: 1.7 }}>
                Feeding A5 anyway would append three constant columns. Its record count is 0 and its status is
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020' }}> not_constructible_data_unavailable</span> — writing "zero gain" is explicitly forbidden.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', marginTop: 12, letterSpacing: 1.2, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>WHAT WE HAVE INSTEAD: A PER-TASK NOISE FLOOR</Text>
            <Table
                style={{ width: 528, height: 108, marginTop: 8 }}
                defaultTextStyle={{ fontSize: 12, textAlign: 'right', color: '#C3D0E2' }}
                defaultCellStyle={{ border: { bottom: { width: 1, color: '#1D2A40' } }, background: { color: '#0E1728' } }}
                cells={[
                    [
                        { text: 'task', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 11, textAlign: 'left' }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                        { text: 'floor |ΔR²|', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 11 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                        { text: 'A3 gain', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 11 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                    ],
                    [{ text: 'pb_t1_tg', textStyle: { textAlign: 'left' } }, '0.0020', { text: '0.0004 below', textStyle: { color: '#FFB020' } }],
                    [{ text: 'pb26_polymetrix_tg', textStyle: { textAlign: 'left' } }, '0.0024', { text: '0.0006 below', textStyle: { color: '#FFB020' } }],
                    [{ text: 'median, 8 tasks', textStyle: { textAlign: 'left', color: '#8FA3BC' } }, { text: '0.0022', textStyle: { color: '#8FA3BC' } }, { text: '6 of 8 clear it', textStyle: { color: '#8FA3BC' } }],
                ]}
            />
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 20px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#4D8DFF', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>H4 · CROSSOVER</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 8, lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                Two properties cross; the third one never does
            </Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 26, marginTop: 14 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>≈ 56</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#8FA3BC', marginTop: 4 }}>Tg · window 355 rows</Text>
                </Box>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>≈ 59</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#8FA3BC', marginTop: 4 }}>dielectric constant · 235 rows</Text>
                </Box>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>none</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#8FA3BC', marginTop: 4 }}>Tm · negative across 30–134</Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 14, lineHeight: 1.7 }}>
                Below roughly 60 training rows the graph arm leads; above it the classical arm leads and stays ahead. That is the
                same fact as "Λ is mostly negative", read from the other end of the axis.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 8, lineHeight: 1.7 }}>
                Three limits, all stated up front: only three properties, descriptive with no significance test, and the three windows
                differ in width — so the two n* values are not comparable with each other.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                Where a window never changes sign, the upper bound is reported and extrapolation stops — no dashed extension is drawn.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>
            null_calibration.csv (48 rows) · openpoly_cpu.csv + openpoly_gpu_index.csv, 225 paired differences
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>13 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
